generated_hash =

// @vibe/compiler/codegen/builtin_bodies — WASM bytecode bodies for the
// linear-backend builtin functions (array/bytes/string/rc primitives, plus
// their `static_*` no-table variants and the wasi `gen_sources_*` embedders)
// (ADR-0070 Phase 3, #897, compiler-internal batch). Compiled into the
// compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv (group `codegen`,
// dual-row: this contract + builtin_bodies.vibe).
//
// The old index.vibe was not the whole implementation: it re-exports all 78
// functions from the sibling bodies_impl.vibe (`export ./bodies_impl.vibe {
// .. }`), which itself is a re-export-only chain down through
// bodies_core_a.vibe/bodies_core_b.vibe -> bodies_core_a1.vibe/a2.vibe ->
// bodies_core_a1a.vibe -> bodies_core_a1a1.vibe -> bodies_core_a1a1_eq.vibe/
// bodies_core_a1a1_str_eq.vibe (plus bodies_core_a1b.vibe) to where the
// functions are actually defined. All 78 leaf signatures are declared here;
// no external file imports any of the bodies_core_*.vibe/bodies_impl.vibe
// siblings directly (verified repo-wide — only the directory form `import
// ../builtin_bodies { .. }` is used), so this directory has no boundary
// spillover the way entry/source_compile and entry/compiler/fs_compile do.
// No exported types (all signatures are Bool/Int/Bytes/Array).

fn gen_eq_body(str_eq_idx: Int) -> Bytes
fn gen_str_eq_body() -> Bytes
fn gen_str_lex_diff_body(enable_rc: Bool) -> Bytes
// #2199: oob_prefix_fat is the operation's message-prefix raw (ptr<<32)|len
// string-table constant, oob_abort_idx the __rt_oob_abort helper's function
// index (prints `<prefix><idx> out of bounds for length <len>` then traps);
// oob_abort_idx < 0 emits the historical bare-trap body (pinned by the
// static twin). Same contract on every bounds-checked builtin below.
